d;text-align:right}@media(max-width:768px){.mw-parser-output .wst-header-mainblock{flex-wrap:wrap}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-central-cell{flex:0 0 100%;order:-2;width:auto}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-back,.mw-parser-output .wst-header-forward{width:auto}}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-notes{display:inline-block;border-collapse:collapse;border-spacing:0;empty-cells:hide;font-size:.9em;line-height:1.4;margin:0 auto 4px auto;width:100%}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-left{float:left}</style><div class=\"ws-header wst-header-structure wst-unknown wst-header ws-header ws-noexport noprint dynlayout-exempt\"><div class=\"wst-header-mainblock wst-unknown-mainblock headertemplate\"><div class=\"wst-header-back searchaux wst-unknown-back\"><div class=\"wst-header-back-arrow\">\u2190</div><div class=\"wst-header-back-link\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Mao_Hsiang\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Mao Hsiang\">Mao Hsiang</a></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-central-cell wst-unknown-central-cell\"><span class=\"wst-header-title wst-unknown-title\"><span class=\"wst-header-title-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1</span><br class=\"wst-header-title-break\" /><span class=\"contributor-text\">edited by&#160;<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Author:Arthur_W._Hummel\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Author:Arthur W. Hummel\">Arthur W. Hummel</a></span></span><div class=\"header-section-text\">Mao I <span class=\"contributor-text\">by&#160;<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Author:Fang_Chao-ying\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Author:Fang Chao-ying\">Fang Chao-ying</a></span></span></div></span></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward searchaux wst-unknown-forward\"><div class=\"wst-header-forward-link\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Mao_Pin\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Mao Pin\">Mao Pin</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367558\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367558\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3646160</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1 \u2014 Mao I</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Fang Chao-ying</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"567\" data-page-number=\"567\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/579\" data-page-index=\"579\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/579\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;579\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>MAO</b> I \u6bdb\u6246 (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u65a7\u5b63), Aug. 13, 1640\u2013after 1710, scholar, native of Ch'ang-shu, Kiangsu, was the youngest son of <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Mao_Chin\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Mao Chin\">Mao Chin</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>]. He inherited the famous library known as Chi-ku-ko (see under his father) and continued the printing business which his father began in 1628. He was also interested in collecting rare texts and writing bibliographical notes, which were much prized by later collectors. Sometime after 1689 he made an inventory of about 500 titles of rare books, including many manuscript facsimiles known as <i>ying-Sung-ch'ao</i> \u5f71\u5b8b\u9214, which it is said he intended to sell to <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/P%27an_Lei\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/P&#39;an Lei\">P'an Lei</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>]. This list, with prices in taels attached, was printed in 1800 in the first installment of the <i>Shih-li-ch\u00fc Huang-shih ts'ung-shu</i> of <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Huang_P%27ei-lieh\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Huang P&#39;ei-lieh\">Huang P'ei-lieh</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>]. Some of the books which he collected bore seals reading \u897f\u6cb3\u5b63\u5b50\u4e4b\u5370 <i>Hsi-ho chi-tz\u016d chih-yin</i> or \u65a7\u5b63\u624b\u6821 <i>Fu-chi shou-chiao</i>. <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ho_Ch%27o\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ho Ch&#39;o\">Ho Ch'o</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] borrowed a number of rare books from Mao I in 1710, and Ho's notes on these items make it certain that Mao was still living at that time. A considerable part of his collection was sold to <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chi_Ch%C3%AAn-i\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chi Ch\u00ean-i\">Chi Ch\u00ean-i</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>].\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[\u7fa9\u9580\u5148\u751f\u96c6 <i>I-men hsien-sh\u00eang chi</i> 9/9a, 12b; see bibliography under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Mao_Chin\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Mao Chin\">Mao Chin</a></span>; Yeh T\u00ea-hui, <i>Shu-lin ch'ing-hua</i> (for char. see bibl. under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chi_Ch%C3%AAn-i\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chi Ch\u00ean-i\">Chi Ch\u00ean-i</a></span>); Yang Li-ch'\u00eang, \u4e2d\u570b\u85cf\u66f8\u5bb6\u8003\u7565 <i>Chung-kuo ts'ang-shu chia k'ao l\u00fceh</i> (1929) p. 7b.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Fang Chao-ying</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Chi Ch\u00ean-i"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ho Ch'o"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Huang P'ei-lieh"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Mao Chin"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Mao Hsiang"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Mao Pin"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/P'an Lei"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Fang Chao-ying"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 1\n | onlysection = mao i\n | previous = Mao Hsiang\n | next     = Mao Pin\n | from     = 579\n | to       = 579\n | notes    =\n | section_author = Fang Chao-ying\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Mao I}}"}}}